    "source_text": "Following general procedure F using 4b (66.8 mg, 0.25 mmol), B2pin2 (127 mg, 0.50 mmol), [Ir(COD)OMe]2 (2.5 mg, 0.00375 mmol) and 1a (3.8 mg, 0.0075 mmol) in THF (1.25 mL). Stirred in vial at 50 °C for 20 hours. Analysis of crude 1 H NMR using internal standard 1,2‐dimethoxyethane showed 22.6:1 meta:para borylation in 94% yield (4% starting material remaining). The crude product was purified by silica gel chromatography (40% EtOAc in Petroleum Ether 40‐60 o C) This gave the title compound (as a 27.1:1:1 mixture of meta:para:st.mat. ratio, as determined by 1 H NMR) as a colourless oil (93 mg). A corrected yield was calculated to account for the 3% starting material in the mixture. Corrected yield – 91 mg, 0.23 mmol, 93%.",
